- op: discuss  # 435f
  at: '2026-07-31T02:15:32Z'  # 435f
  by: agent  # 435f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 435f
  clock: 3  # 435f
  nonce: 435f  # 435f
  message: "Fixed in PR #107, merged to dev 1cc89c7170. No governance change was required.\n\nTHE DEFECT IS REAL AND THE MECHANISM IS AS FILED. tests/_forge_github_harness.py:205 prepended the fake bindir to PATH rather than replacing it, so bindir_with_fakes(gh=False) left /usr/bin/gh reachable, scripts/contribute:240's `command -v gh` probe succeeded, and TestGitHubFallbackWhenGhAbsent ran with gh present -- the real binary calling api.github.com/graphql and failing HTTP 401.\n\nBUT THIS ITEM OVER-STATED IT THREE WAYS, all corrected in the CHANGELOG:\n\n1. \"19 call sites share the premise\" -- wrong unit. There is exactly ONE `command -v gh` probe in the whole scripts/ tree (contribute:240) and exactly ONE failing test. The 19 counted uses of the helper, not exposure to the defect. Every other github-arm test never probes gh, so gh's presence is irrelevant to them.\n\n2. \"on a machine with valid gh auth ... it would create a real pull request against the fixture's up/r upstream\" -- overstated. _GH_UP is the placeholder https://github.com/up/r.git, so an authenticated run produces an API error, not a PR.\n\n3. Candidate (b) as filed (\"add a gh shim that simulates absence\") is unworkable and the item half-suspected it. `command -v` is satisfied by any executable shim; a directory or dangling symlink named gh is skipped and the lookup continues to the real one. Confirmed rather than left as a maybe.\n\nWHAT WAS UNDER-STATED, and is the part that actually mattered: the credential scrub list popped FORGEJO_TOKEN, SELFHOSTED_FORGEJO_TOKEN and HG_GITHUB_TOKEN -- none of which gh reads -- while omitting GH_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN and GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN, which it does. All three were unset where this was found, which is the only reason the failure was an unauthenticated 401 rather than an authenticated client acting under a real token. Now scrubbed.\n\nFIX SHIPPED: candidate (a). The harness builds a shadow directory -- one symlink per executable on the inherited PATH, minus gh, built once per process (~400ms, 2742 links here) -- and runs scripts with the fake bindir followed by that shadow. Replacing PATH is the only formulation under which \"no fake gh was requested\" and \"gh cannot be found\" are the same statement; gh lives in /usr/bin beside git/sed/awk, so filtering its directory would take the script's real dependencies with it. The alternative -- an AUTO_PR_SIMULATE_*-style env seam in scripts/contribute -- was rejected: it puts a test-only branch in production code AND scripts/contribute is a governance file. The harness-only fix needs neither, which is why this closed without an approval round.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE on merged dev:\n    gh reachable from harness PATH  : False   (was True)\n    git reachable                    : True\n    GH_TOKEN present in child env    : False   (was True)\n    test_contribute_github + test_forge_github_harness + test_smart_test : 17 passed\n    full root suite                  : 1427 passed (was 1426 passed / 1 failed)\n\nTests pin the GUARANTEE, not any single caller, because the failure mode is silent -- an un-faked tool simply works. Five cases including the positive control that a requested fake gh still resolves (isolation that broke gh=True would trade one silent wrong branch for another) and a check that git actually RUNS rather than merely resolving.\n\nCARRIED OUT OF SCOPE, because this fix could not otherwise be verified in CI at all: smart-test now always runs a test file you edited, root tests included. Two compounding defects -- the changed-test pattern covered only packages/*/tests/, and the check sat inside the TDD fallback that fires only when nothing else was selected, so an edited root test alongside any mapped source was silently dropped. Now computed once and unioned unconditionally. scripts/smart-test had NO tests at all; tests/test_smart_test.py starts that coverage by extracting the live regex from the script rather than restating it.\n\nThat makes four independent routes to one failure across this cycle (WI-libok's misnamed test file, WI-bisar's 1:1 map, and both halves of this one). The class: a test that cannot be selected is indistinguishable from a test that passes, and the tool that decides selection was itself ungated."  # 435f
